R-SO9 R-SO10 R-TF1 R-TF3 R-TF6 (slice 022b): the launcher test of the `roc` on PATH, with the fake Fx. 2 runs of `install` with `TALON_NIGHTLY=0`, so the gate names the id of the roc on PATH (exit 10) before any probe.
Run 1: the cache is missing. The walk reads the cache, hashes `launcher/roc` and then tln (equal, so it is the launcher), hashes `old/roc` (same size, other bytes: not the launcher), runs `<path> version` once, and writes the cache. `later/roc` and `small/roc` are never hashed and never run (the first compiler wins). The text of the gate names `nightly-2026-10-13-91fa0c2`.
Run 2: the same state. The cache has the rows, so there is no hash and no `roc version`: the calls are `path_roc` and one `read_files`, and there is no write. The same text.
The files of the cache are not in `tree.diff` (the runner leaves out `path-roc.json`, its size and mtime come from the machine). The text of the file is in the L0 file `tests/unit/pathroc.roc` and in the L3 case `compilers/so9-launcher`.
